menu "EPDiy"

    config EPD_ESP32S3_I80_ROW_OUTPUT
        bool "ESP32-S3: row-by-row output over the LCD_CAM i80 bus (shift-register boards)"
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
        default n
        help
            The default ESP32-S3 render method streams whole frames through the LCD_CAM
            peripheral and needs the latch (LEH) and vertical start (STV) lines on real GPIOs.

            Some boards (for example the LILYGO T5-4.7 S3 "V2.3"/"V2.4") drive LEH, STV,
            output enable, mode and the panel power rails through a 74HCT4094 shift register
            instead. Those boards need the older, row-by-row render method that latches every
            row through the board's set_ctrl() callback, which epdiy so far only had for the
            original ESP32 (I2S peripheral).

            Enable this option to use that render method on the ESP32-S3, with the pixel data
            of each row sent over the LCD_CAM peripheral in i80 mode. Leave it disabled for
            all boards that wire the control lines to GPIOs (epd_board_v7 and similar).

endmenu
